<title>BELGIUM: EU urges Italy to focus on spending cuts - diplomat.</title>
<headline>EU urges Italy to focus on spending cuts - diplomat.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union finance ministers urged Italy on Monday to focus less on new taxes as a way of lowering its deficits and more on cutting spending, an EU diplomat said.</p>
<p>The diplomat said the ministers, meeting to discuss Italy's programme to qualifying for monetary union, had urged Rome to focus on reforming its social security and pension systems. -- Brussels Newsroom: +32 2 287-6830</p>
</text>
